#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:9
msgid ""
"Machines manages the QEMU/KVM virtual machines of a libvirt connection, the "
"system one or your user session, built with GTK 4 and libadwaita."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:11
msgid ""
"Start, shut down, pause, save to disk, reboot and force off machines, and "
"follow their state as it changes"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:12
msgid ""
"A built-in VNC and SPICE console that scales the guest's display to the "
"window and passes the keyboard and pointer through, with sound, clipboard "
"sharing, USB redirection and 3D acceleration over SPICE"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:13
msgid "A serial console shown as text"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:14
msgid ""
"New machines from an installation ISO or an existing disk image, with a disk "
"in libvirt's default storage pool, set up for the system on the ISO"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:15
msgid ""
"Processors, memory, autostart, boot order and the CD-ROM drive changed from "
"the details page"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:16
msgid ""
"Graphs of what a running machine uses of the host's processors, memory, "
"disks and network"
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.sachesi.machines.metainfo.xml:17
msgid ""
"Processor model, topology and pinning, huge pages, and BIOS or UEFI firmware "
